\newlabel{sec:app-tables}{{A}{9}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces Reference model (Gemini-3.6-Flash): accuracy (\%) with the image and with text only, the paired difference, the share of swapped-image answers equal to the donor's key, and the donor-tracking gain (percentage points). Accuracy is over all items (AIA 46, LIL 38, DSCR 46); the swap and donor-key columns use the donor-paired items (AIA 46, LIL 38, DSCR 42).}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ctrl}{{IV}{10}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces E2: share of answers (\%) that equal the donor's key when the image is swapped, and when there is no image; the gain is the difference in percentage points, with its bootstrap interval, an add-half sparse-data interval (Add-half CI) and the exact McNemar $p$ (unadjusted); the last column is the share of items whose answer differs from the own-image answer after the swap. Sample sizes are the donor-paired items (AIA 46, LIL 38, DSCR 42); the own-image accuracy in Table~\ref {tab:e1} is over all items (DSCR 46).}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e2}{{V}{10}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VI}{\ignorespaces DSCR class-wise confusion for Llama-4-Scout with its own image (rows: the item's RANO key class; columns: the model's predicted class; recall on the diagonal). Overall accuracy 54.3{}\% is below the majority share (58.7{}\%), but the model is not a constant predictor: it recovers 6{} of 19{} non-majority items while missing some progressive-disease items, so below-majority accuracy is not evidence that the slice is unread.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:confusion}{{VI}{10}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VII}{\ignorespaces Diagnostics on the DSCR donor swap (42{} recipients), run on synthetic predictors with known behaviour over 50{} simulations: the donor-tracking gain, the image-vs-text answer-change rate, and the share of simulations in which the permutation flags tracking ($p<.05$). A generic image shift that ignores which donor is shown reaches a positive gain and a high answer-change rate yet is never flagged, and at $\rho =0.4$ a genuine tracker and the generic shift share the same gain (+19.0{} vs +19.0{}~pp): neither the gain nor the answer-change rate separates them, the permutation does.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:donorval}{{VII}{10}{}{}{}}
